            {
              "id": "491688ca-9496-469e-8e6c-01c8526b3128",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Play Reconsidered: Sociological Perspectives on Human Expression</strong></em> was written by Thomas S. Henricks, published by University of Illinois Press, July 11, 2006."
            },
            {
              "id": "7a7c3455-b22d-493a-a257-53a3d8f04092",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "04a86b0f-3ae8-4b36-8a29-408e92da0780",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Arguing that play is a social and cultural phenomenon of adult life, enveloped by wider structures and processes of society, this work explores </em><a href=\"#/communism\"><em>Karl Marx</em></a><em>'s analysis of creativity in human labour, examines Emile Durkheim's observations on the role of </em><a href=\"#/ritual\"><em>ritual</em></a><em> and the formation of collective consciousness, and more.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "8e235f45-fad1-4af1-bcc6-6291e36b9bf2",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            }
